<title>UK: Signet Group says H1 pre-tax loss narrows.</title>
<headline>Signet Group says H1 pre-tax loss narrows.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to August 3, 1996</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		7.3 loss	     vs 11.3 loss</p>
<p> Pretax loss		6.0		    vs 21.3</p>
<p> Turnover		   369.61		 vs 344.91</p>
<p> Operating result	 9.97		   vs 2.87 loss</p>
<p> Interest payable	 15.92		  vs 18.47</p>
<p> Tax paid		   1.80		   vs 6.40</p>
<p> Attributable	     4.16 loss	    vs 14.90 loss</p>
<p>NOTE - Signet Group Plc, formerly Ratners, is a retailer of jewellery, watches and gifts trading in the UK as H.Samuel and Ernest Jones and in the U.S. as Sterling.</p>
<p>It said improved results at the half year were encouraging but the outcome for the year as a whole would be dependent on Thanksgiving and Christmas trading.  </p>
<p>Signet said its net debt at August 3, 1996 was 306.1 million stg, a reduction of 36.8 million compared to the interim stage last year. It said discussions on the sale of its UK jewellery business were continuing with one potential buyer.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
